  "notes": [
    "Scanning the proxy's Upgraded topic from deployment to the exploit block returns exactly four events: 0x5a02541cb59efcc23c581f8d6599fc9810e7ea50 at block 69852042 (the proxy's own creation) and again at 74633620, 0xfd28a6e45402a4322fed47f883b765f03327b36e at 76558148, and 0x9153e149b0d90dea634ed9f7df6ff71c2109b654 at 76904623 log 398. The EIP-1967 implementation slot holds 0xfd28a6e4 at block 76904622 and 0x9153e149 at the pre-exploit block 84938855. Implementation 0x9153e149 was deployed 8 seconds earlier at block 76904619 and its runtime hashes to 0x42b0e9fb7741fa038dbf6c64f2167c84c9136502f2364afb0c7514caa35bea2a identically at blocks 76904619, 76904623 and 84938855.",
    "Victim depletion is the CES reserve of the Whalebit pricer 0xb5ea1d17f3d8da34a6d6a1d2acc2a148e1411868, which held 3860529.112155042786446303 CES at block 84938855 and 3764.900981724002319963 CES at block 84938891, the block of the last successful campaign transaction: an exact delta of 3856764.211173318784126340 CES. Netting every CES Transfer log in blocks 84938856-84938891 confirms the destination split to the wei: 3480231.008245918711348953 CES to the attacker's cash-out address 0x48880b3dd87638e5ea75905c3a150e8a3aa6cda9 by way of the attack contract, 327410.568602360 CES absorbed by the CES/USDT Algebra pool as price impact, 45966.219626878 CES to the flash-loan pool 0x296b95dd0e8b726c4e358b0683ff0b6d675c35e9 as its fee, and about 3158 CES to ordinary user withdrawals in the same window. The attacker supplied no CES of its own: the attack contract's CES balance is zero at block 84938855 and every CES it used came from the flash loan, which was repaid in each transaction. CES cannot be marked at spot: the whole CES/USDT pool held only 506592.192894 USDT against 1172329.719850312269562891 CES before the attack, so the DefiLlama spot of 1.0794181571885721 USD would value the depletion at 4.16 million USD that could never have been realised. The evidenced price is what the attacker actually got: it moved 3480230.179742374772846706 CES through swap helper 0x63242a4ea82847b20e506b63b0e2e2eff0cc6cb0 in 43 tranches between blocks 84938903 and 84940699 and received 670659.427635127488882569 DAI, 113829.474698 USDC and 39720.849160 USDT back, 824209.751493127488882569 USD at par, an average of 0.2368262180733517 USD per CES. That average is applied to the full gross depletion here, which is why the recorded figure of 913382.88 USD exceeds the 824209.75 USD the attacker kept; the difference is the CES the pools took as slippage and flash fee, which METHODOLOGY does not deduct from gross victim depletion. The seed row's 824000 USD figure is the attacker's realised proceeds rounded. A later 113829.474698 USDC transfer into the cash-out address from 0x9295ee1d8c5b022be115a2ad3c30c72e34e7f096 at block 84946849 is a downstream reshuffle of funds that address had already sent out and is not counted twice. No recovery was identified.",
    "The staking implementation 0x9153e149b0d90dea634ed9f7df6ff71c2109b654 and the pricer implementation 0x0729ea061132bcd76f420f9139af8957b41b90cb are unverified on Polygonscan, so the root cause is established from the call trace, the emitted Deposit and Withdraw values and the two price reads rather than from source. Only the level table implementation 0x35952dd1d135215cb22c07ae956ee02d4793023b is verified, and it contains no oracle: getPriceForLevel returns owner-set storage."
